[{"code":"list_still_used","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/inline/ListPrependShared.beni","start":{"line":14,"col":19},"end":{"line":14,"col":29}},"title":"LIST CHANGED WHILE STILL IN USE","message":"`[ …xs, 7 ]` adds to the end of `xs` itself, but `xs` is read again afterwards.\n\n14|        , summary [ …xs, 7 ]\n                     ^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n15|        , summary (xs ++ [ 7 ])\n                      ^^ and `xs` is read here, after the change\n\nIf the list were changed in place, `xs` would see the change when it is read on\nline 15.\n\nTo change a copy and leave `xs` as it was, copy it there:\n\n14|        , summary [ …List.copy xs, 7 ]\n\nThis is sharing the checker can see: `xs` is read on line 15, after the change."},{"code":"list_still_used","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/inline/ListPrependShared.beni","start":{"line":15,"col":20},"end":{"line":15,"col":31}},"title":"LIST CHANGED WHILE STILL IN USE","message":"`xs ++ [ 7 ]` adds to the end of `xs` itself, but `xs` is read again afterwards.\n\n15|        , summary (xs ++ [ 7 ])\n                      ^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n16|        , summary (List.append xs [ 8 ])\n                                  ^^ and `xs` is read here, after the change\n\nIf the list were changed in place, `xs` would see the change when it is read on\nline 16.\n\nTo change a copy and leave `xs` as it was, copy it there:\n\n15|        , summary (List.copy xs ++ [ 7 ])\n\nThis is sharing the checker can see: `xs` is read on line 16, after the change."},{"code":"list_still_used","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/inline/ListPrependShared.beni","start":{"line":16,"col":20},"end":{"line":16,"col":40}},"title":"LIST CHANGED WHILE STILL IN USE","message":"`List.append` changes `xs` in place, but `xs` is read again afterwards.\n\n16|        , summary (List.append xs [ 8 ])\n                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n17|        , summary xs\n                     ^^ and `xs` is read here, after the change\n\nIf the list were changed in place, `xs` would see the change when it is read on\nline 17.\n\nTo change a copy and leave `xs` as it was, copy it there:\n\n16|        , summary (List.append (List.copy xs) [ 8 ])\n\nThis is sharing the checker can see: `xs` is read on line 17, after the change."}]
